Q3. Differentiate between BeanFactory and ApplicationContext.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ANSWER:

+----------------------+------------------------------+-----------------------------------+
| Feature              | BeanFactory                  | ApplicationContext                 |
+----------------------+------------------------------+-----------------------------------+
| Package              | org.springframework.beans    | org.springframework.context        |
| Bean Initialization  | Lazy (on first request)      | Eager (at startup)                 |
| Annotation Support   | No                           | Yes (@Autowired, @Component, etc.) |
| Event Publishing     | Not supported                | Supported (ApplicationEvent)       |
| i18n Support         | Not supported                | Supported (MessageSource)          |
| AOP Integration      | Limited                      | Full support                       |
| Usage                | Lightweight / Unit tests     | Recommended for production use     |
+----------------------+------------------------------+-----------------------------------+

Example:
  // BeanFactory
  BeanFactory factory = new XmlBeanFactory(new ClassPathResource("beans.xml"));

  // ApplicationContext
  ApplicationContext ctx = new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("beans.xml");

CONCLUSION: ApplicationContext is the preferred choice in Spring MVC
            applications as it provides full enterprise features.


