Q4. Explain how JdbcTemplate simplifies JDBC operations.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ANSWER:

Problems with Plain JDBC:
  -> Developer must manually open connection, create statement,
     execute query, handle ResultSet, close connection, and handle exceptions.
  -> Very verbose and error-prone.

How JdbcTemplate Helps:
  -> JdbcTemplate is a Spring class that wraps all the boilerplate JDBC code.
  -> It handles: Connection opening/closing, Exception handling,
                 Statement creation, ResultSet processing.

COMPARISON:

  Without JdbcTemplate (plain JDBC):
  ----------------------------------
  Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, pass);
  PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement("SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=?");
  ps.setInt(1, id);
  ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery();
  if(rs.next()) { ... }
  rs.close(); ps.close(); con.close();

  With JdbcTemplate:
  ------------------
  String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?";
  User user = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject(sql, new BeanPropertyRowMapper<>(User.class), id);

Key JdbcTemplate Methods:
  -> queryForObject()  -- fetch single object
  -> query()           -- fetch list of objects
  -> update()          -- INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE
  -> execute()         -- run DDL statements

Benefits:
  -> Reduces lines of code significantly
  -> Spring manages connection automatically
  -> Checked SQLExceptions converted to unchecked DataAccessException


