Q5. Explain the role of DispatcherServlet in Spring MVC.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ANSWER:

DispatcherServlet is the FRONT CONTROLLER in Spring MVC.
It acts as the central entry point for all HTTP requests.

Role of DispatcherServlet:

  1. Receives Request:
     -> All incoming requests are first intercepted by DispatcherServlet.

  2. Consults HandlerMapping:
     -> Finds which Controller method should handle this request (based on URL).

  3. Calls Controller:
     -> Delegates the request to the appropriate Controller.

  4. Handles Model and View:
     -> Gets the logical view name returned by the Controller.

  5. Consults ViewResolver:
     -> Resolves logical view name to physical view file (e.g., .jsp).

  6. Renders Response:
     -> Sends the final rendered view back to the browser.

Configuration in web.xml:
  <servlet>
      <servlet-name>dispatcher</servlet-name>
      <servlet-class>org.springframework.web.servlet.DispatcherServlet</servlet-class>
      <load-on-startup>1</load-on-startup>
  </servlet>
  <servlet-mapping>
      <servlet-name>dispatcher</servlet-name>
      <url-pattern>/</url-pattern>
  </servlet-mapping>

SUMMARY: DispatcherServlet coordinates all components of Spring MVC like a
         traffic controller, directing requests to the right handlers.


